# Certificates recording what a gate or published-image validation proved.
# commit-gate-stamp.sh writes the tree certificate checked by pre-commit;
# image-candidate.sh writes digest-bound image-candidate receipts consumed
# by edge promotion. They describe one clone's validation state, so they are
# never committed — but the directory is, so a fresh clone has somewhere to put
# them and this rule is in force before the first certificate is written.
#
# The rule is load-bearing, not tidiness. A certificate is a hash of the working
# tree; a *tracked* certificate would be part of the tree it measures, so writing
# one would change the answer and no certificate could ever match twice. The
# script refuses to write a certificate that git does not ignore, so if this rule
# is ever edited away the gate fails loudly instead of silently rejecting every
# commit.
*
!.gitignore
